REM Protects statements whose trailing option tail is order-independent at the compiler even
REM though the grammar used to fix one order, plus a verb that previously had no grammar rule at
REM all. Covers the verb bare, with its option tail in either written order, with a single option,
REM and with no spaces around the option separators, in upper, lower and mixed case.

SETDRIVE "C:\bbj"
setdrive "C:\bbj"
SetDrive "C:\bbj"
SETDRIVE "C:\bbj",ERR=driveerr
driveerr: END
